{"step_index":732,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-24T04:38:32Z","content":"# 🛠️ Complete Tech Stack of **CodeDuel**\n\n**CodeDuel** is built as a production-grade, real-time full-stack competitive programming and 1v1 Versus platform. Here is the complete breakdown of technologies, frameworks, and architecture used across the application:\n\n---\n\n## 🎨 1. Frontend Technologies\n\n| Category | Technology | Purpose & Implementation |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Core Framework** | **React.js (v18)** | Component-based UI with React Hooks (`useState`, `useEffect`, `useRef`, `useCallback`, `useContext`) |\n| **Build Tool** | **Vite (v5)** | Lightning-fast HMR (Hot Module Replacement), optimized ES modules, and production bundling |\n| **Code Editor** | **Monaco Editor** (`@monaco-editor/react`) | VS Code's core editor with syntax highlighting, bracket matching, tab handling, shortcuts (`Ctrl+Enter` to submit), and multi-language support |\n| **Styling & Design** | **Tailwind CSS (v3)** | Cyberpunk dark aesthetic, glassmorphism, responsive grid systems, animated glowing badges, and custom typography |\n| **Routing** | **React Router DOM (v6)** | Client-side routing, protected routes (`/duel/:matchId`, `/practice`, `/leaderboard`, `/profile`, `/match/:id/analysis`) |\n| **Real-Time Client** | **STOMP over SockJS** (`@stomp/stompjs`, `sockjs-client`) | Bi-directional WebSocket communication for live matchmaking, duel state sync, countdowns, opponent typing indicators, and instant verdict alerts |\n| **HTTP Client** | **Axios** | REST API calls with request/response interceptors for automatic JWT attachment and 401 handling |\n| **Icons** | **Lucide React** (`lucide-react`) | Clean, modern vector icons for UI buttons, badges, metrics, and navigation |\n| **Audio Synthesis** | **HTML5 Web Audio API** | Procedural sound effects (match found chime, countdown ticks, victory fanfare, error buzzer) without external audio files |\n| **State Persistence** | **Browser LocalStorage** | Stores JWT auth tokens, user sessions, draft codes, and persistent programming language preferences (**Java / C++ / Python / JS**) |\n\n---\n\n## ⚙️ 2. Backend Technologies\n\n| Category | Technology | Purpose & Implementation |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Language & Runtime** | **Java 17 (OpenJDK 17)** | Modern LTS Java runtime utilizing pattern matching, records, streams, and virtual thread readiness |\n| **Backend Framework** | **Spring Boot (v3.2.5)** | Enterprise REST API and WebSocket micro-architecture with auto-configuration and dependency injection |\n| **Security & Auth** | **Spring Security 6 + JJWT** | Stateless JWT authentication, role-based access control (`ROLE_USER`, `ROLE_ADMIN`), BCrypt password hashing, CORS filters |\n| **Real-Time Server** | **Spring WebSocket + Spring Messaging** | STOMP message broker with `/app` application destination prefix and `/topic`, `/queue` broadcast channels |\n| **ORM & Data Access** | **Spring Data JPA / Hibernate 6** | Entity modeling, repository layer, custom JPQL queries, automatic schema migration, and transaction management (`@Transactional`) |\n| **Primary Database** | **MySQL 8.0+** | Relational database for persistent storage of users, 1,000 problems, 5,000 test cases, match histories, and rating logs |\n| **Embedded DB (Dev/Test)** | **H2 Database** | In-memory relational database for zero-config local development and rapid integration testing |\n| **Caching & Fast Lookups** | **Redis (Spring Data Redis / Lettuce)** | Caching user sessions, leaderboard ranking caches, and matchmaking queue state |\n| **Logging** | **SLF4J + Logback** | Structured logging for judge executions, match lifecycles, and security events |\n| **Testing Suite** | **JUnit 5 + Mockito + Spring Boot Test** | Unit and integration testing for judge execution, Elo calculations, efficiency scoring, and full 1,000-question catalog integrity |\n\n---\n\n## ⚡ 3. Online Judge & Execution Engine (Custom Built)\n\n| Component | Technology | Description |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Execution Sandbox** | **`ExecutionSandbox.java`** | Isolated process execution sandbox using `ProcessBuilder` with per-submission directory isolation, memory capping (256MB), and strict execution time limits (2000–3000ms) |\n| **Java Execution** | **`javac` + Reflection Wrapper** | Compiles user code and executes it via dynamic reflection to seamlessly inspect parameter types (`int[]`, `String`, `int`, `boolean`) and match output formats |\n| **C++ Execution** | **`g++ -O2 -std=c++17`** | High-performance C++ compiler with optimization flags |\n| **Python Execution** | **Python 3.11 + `inspect.signature`** | Dynamic argument introspection and execution |\n| **JavaScript Execution** | **Node.js 20** | V8 engine JavaScript execution |\n| **Efficiency Engine** | **`EfficiencyEngine.java`** | Proprietary algorithm computing 0–100 score based on execution time percentile, memory footprint, code length, and AST loop nesting |\n| **Complexity Estimator** | **`ComplexityEstimator.java`** | Static code analysis heuristic predicting time complexity (\\(O(1)\\), \\(O(\\log n)\\), \\(O(n)\\), \\(O(n \\log n)\\), \\(O(n^2)\\)) |\n\n---\n\n## 🎮 4. Competitive Game Logic & Systems\n\n* **Matchmaking Engine (`MatchmakingService.java`)**:\n  * Real-time Elo bracket grouping with expanding search windows over time.\n  * Instant fallback algorithm pairing users when queue times exceed thresholds.\n  * Thread-safe concurrency handling to prevent duplicate match assignments.\n* **Rating System (`EloRatingService.java`)**:\n  * Standard FIDE/competitive programming Elo formula: \\(R' = R + K \\cdot (S - E)\\).\n  * Dynamic K-factors based on experience and rating tiers (Novice, Apprentice, Specialist, Expert, Master, Grandmaster).\n  * Win streak multipliers and bonus points for high efficiency scores.\n* **1,000 Question Bank & 5,000 Testcases (`ProblemSeeder.java`)**:\n  * 16 DSA categories (Arrays, Two Pointers, Binary Search, Trees, Graphs, DP, etc.).\n  * 3-tier editorials (Brute Force, Better, Most Optimal) with interview tips.\n  * Dedicated Java & C++ solutions.\n* **Gamification & Achievements (`AchievementService.java`)**:\n  * Real-time badge unlocking for streaks, rating milestones, speed demon submissions, and perfect efficiency runs.","thinking":"**Examining CodeDuel's Tech**\n\nI'm currently focused on dissecting the CodeDuel application's tech stack. I've begun to break down the frontend, noting its reliance on React 18 with React Hooks and Context. Next, I'll examine the backend, data storage, and deployment infrastructure to gain a full perspective.\n\n\n**Analyzing Frontend Features**\n\nI've been taking a deep dive into CodeDuel's frontend, and now I'm shifting my focus to its feature set. Specifically, I'm focusing on the component libraries. This includes Vite, Tailwind CSS with its custom dark theme and responsive grid layout. I'm also examining the code editor, which leverages `@monaco-editor/react`, and the routing setup using React Router DOM v6. I've also identified the real-time communication strategy, incorporating STOMP over SockJS for WebSocket messaging, and the use of Lucide React for icons.\n\n\n**Investigating Backend Architecture**\n\nI'm now focusing on the backend, and there's a lot to unpack. Java 17 and Spring Boot 3.2.5 form the core of the application. I'm noting the use of Spring Web MVC for the RESTful API, with structured DTO responses. Spring Security 6 handles authentication using JWTs and BCrypt. Real-time aspects are managed by Spring WebSocket with STOMP, while Spring Data JPA and Hibernate 6 manage data persistence, primarily with MySQL in production, and H2 for testing. Caching is handled by Redis.\n\n\n"}
