{"step_index":749,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-24T04:42:32Z","thinking":"**Initiating PDF Design**\n\nI've successfully installed `reportlab`! My focus now shifts to crafting a Python script that will generate a PDF. I envision it being titled \"CodeDuel - Comprehensive Interview Preparation & System Architecture Guide.pdf.\" I'm also planning a professional layout with a header.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"CodeContent":"import os\nfrom reportlab.lib.pagesizes import letter\nfrom reportlab.lib import colors\nfrom reportlab.platypus import (\n    SimpleDocTemplate, Paragraph, Spacer, Table, TableStyle, PageBreak, KeepTogether, HRFlowable\n)\nfrom reportlab.lib.styles import getSampleStyleSheet, ParagraphStyle\nfrom reportlab.pdfgen import canvas\n\nclass NumberedCanvas(canvas.Canvas):\n    def __init__(self, *args, **kwargs):\n        super(NumberedCanvas, self).__init__(*args, **kwargs)\n        self._saved_page_states = []\n\n    def showPage(self):\n        self._saved_page_states.append(dict(self.__dict__))\n        self._startPage()\n\n    def save(self):\n        num_pages = len(self._saved_page_states)\n        for state in self._saved_page_states:\n            self.__dict__.update(state)\n            self.draw_page_decorations(num_pages)\n            super(NumberedCanvas, self).showPage()\n        super(NumberedCanvas, self).save()\n\n    def draw_page_decorations(self, page_count):\n        self.saveState()\n        self.setFont(\"Helvetica\", 9)\n        self.setFillColor(colors.HexColor(\"#64748b\"))\n        \n        # Header (pages 2+)\n        if self._pageNumber > 1:\n            self.drawString(54, 11 * 72 - 36, \"CodeDuel — Complete Technical Interview & Architecture Guide\")\n            self.setStrokeColor(colors.HexColor(\"#cbd5e1\"))\n            self.setLineWidth(0.5)\n            self.line(54, 11 * 72 - 42, 8.5 * 72 - 54, 11 * 72 - 42)\n        \n        # Footer\n        self.setStrokeColor(colors.HexColor(\"#cbd5e1\"))\n        self.setLineWidth(0.5)\n        self.line(54, 48, 8.5 * 72 - 54, 48)\n        \n        self.drawString(54, 34, \"Confidential & Proprietary • Full-Stack Competitive Programming Platform\")\n        page_text = f\"Page {self._pageNumber} of {page_count}\"\n        self.drawRightString(8.5 * 72 - 54, 34, page_text)\n        self.restoreState()\n\ndef generate_pdf():\n    pdf_path = r\"C:\\Users\\rajan\\.gemini\\antigravity\\scratch\\codeduel\\CodeDuel_Interview_Preparation_Guide.pdf\"\n    \n    doc = SimpleDocTemplate(\n        pdf_path,\n        pagesize=letter,\n        leftMargin=54,\n        rightMargin=54,\n        topMargin=54,\n        bottomMargin=54\n    )\n    \n    styles = getSampleStyleSheet()\n    \n    # Custom styles\n    primary_color = colors.HexColor(\"#1e1b4b\")  # Deep indigo\n    accent_blue = colors.HexColor(\"#0284c7\")    # Cyan/Blue\n    accent_emerald = colors.HexColor(\"#059669\") # Emerald\n    text_dark = colors.HexColor(\"#0f172a\")      # Slate 900\n    text_muted = colors.HexColor(\"#475569\")     # Slate 600\n    code_bg = colors.HexColor(\"#f8fafc\")        # Slate 50\n    \n    title_style = ParagraphStyle(\n        'DocTitle',\n        parent=styles['Heading1'],\n        fontName='Helvetica-Bold',\n        fontSize=24,\n        leading=28,\n        textColor=colors.white,\n        alignment=1, # Center\n        spaceAfter=6\n    )\n    \n    subtitle_style = ParagraphStyle(\n        'DocSubtitle',\n        parent=styles['Normal'],\n        fontName='Helvetica',\n        fontSize=12,\n        leading=16,\n        textColor=colors.HexColor(\"#93c5fd\"),\n        alignment=1,\n        spaceAfter=0\n    )\n    \n    h1_style = ParagraphStyle(\n        'Heading1_Custom',\n        fontName='Helvetica-Bold',\n        fontSize=16,\n        leading=20,\n        textColor=primary_color,\n        spaceBefore=14,\n        spaceAfter=8,\n        keepWithNext=True\n    )\n    \n    h2_style = ParagraphStyle(\n        'Heading2_Custom',\n        fontName='Helvetica-Bold',\n        fontSize=12,\n        leading=16,\n        textColor=accent_blue,\n        spaceBefore=10,\n        spaceAfter=4,\n        keepWithNext=True\n    )\n    \n    body_style = ParagraphStyle(\n        'Body_Custom',\n        fontName='Helvetica',\n        fontSize=9.5,\n        leading=14,\n        textColor=text_dark,\n        spaceAfter=6\n    )\n    \n    bullet_style = ParagraphStyle(\n        'Bullet_Custom',\n        fontName='Helvetica',\n        fontSize=9,\n        leading=13.5,\n        textColor=text_dark,\n        leftIndent=15,\n        spaceAfter=4\n    )\n    \n    q_style = ParagraphStyle(\n        'Question_Style',\n        fontName='Helvetica-Bold',\n        fontSize=10.5,\n        leading=14.5,\n        textColor=colors.HexColor(\"#1e293b\"),\n        spaceBefore=8,\n        spaceAfter=4,\n        keepWithNext=True\n    )\n    \n    ans_style = ParagraphStyle(\n        'Answer_Style',\n        fontName='Helvetica',\n        fontSize=9,\n        leading=13.5,\n        textColor=colors.HexColor(\"#334155\"),\n        spaceAfter=6\n    )\n\n    callout_style = ParagraphStyle(\n        'Callout_Style',\n        fontName='Helvetica-Oblique',\n        fontSize=9,\n        leading=13,\n        textColor=colors.HexColor(\"#0369a1\")\n    )\n    \n    story = []\n    \n    # 1. Header Banner\n    banner_data = [\n        [\n            Paragraph(\"⚔️ CODEDUEL\", title_style),\n        ],\n        [\n            Paragraph(\"Full-Stack 1v1 Competitive Programming Platform<br/>Comprehensive Interview Preparation & System Architecture Guide\", subtitle_style)\n        ]\n    ]\n    banner_table = Table(banner_data, colWidths=[504])\n    banner_table.setStyle(TableStyle([\n        ('BACKGROUND', (0,0), (-1,-1), colors.HexColor(\"#1e1b4b\")),\n        ('TOPPADDING', (0,0), (-1,-1), 16),\n        ('BOTTOMPADDING', (0,0), (-1,-1), 16),\n        ('LEFTPADDING', (0,0), (-1,-1), 16),\n        ('RIGHTPADDING', (0,0), (-1,-1), 16),\n        ('ALIGN', (0,0), (-1,-1), 'CENTER'),\n        ('VALIGN', (0,0), (-1,-1), 'MIDDLE'),\n        ('CORNERPAD', (0,0), (-1,-1), 8),\n    ]))\n    story.append(banner_table)\n    story.append(Spacer(1, 14))\n    \n    # 2. Executive Overview\n    story.append(Paragraph(\"1. Executive Summary & Core Value Proposition\", h1_style))\n    story.append(Paragraph(\n        \"<b>CodeDuel</b> is an enterprise-grade, real-time 1v1 competitive programming platform inspired by modern Versus gaming experiences. \"\n        \"Unlike traditional asynchronous problem archives (e.g. LeetCode / HackerRank), CodeDuel matches two engineers of balanced skill ratings (Elo), \"\n        \"synchronizes a live countdown, provides the exact same algorithmic problem, and orchestrates a real-time race where users code, submit, \"\n        \"receive instant multi-language sandbox verdicts, and get rewarded with dynamic rating adjustments and in-depth performance analytics.\",\n        body_style\n    ))\n    story.append(Spacer(1, 6))\n    \n    # Tech Stack Summary Table\n    story.append(Paragraph(\"2. Complete Technology Stack Matrix\", h1_style))\n    stack_data = [\n        [Paragraph(\"<b>Layer</b>\", body_style), Paragraph(\"<b>Technologies Used</b>\", body_style), Paragraph(\"<b>Key Responsibilities</b>\", body_style)],\n        [\n            Paragraph(\"<b>Frontend UI</b>\", body_style),\n            Paragraph(\"React 18, Vite, Tailwind CSS, Monaco Editor\", body_style),\n            Paragraph(\"Responsive cyber dark UI, Monaco code editor, live typing broadcasts, multi-tab problem explorer (Description, 3-Tier Editorial, Solutions, Hints)\", body_style)\n        ],\n        [\n            Paragraph(\"<b>Real-Time Web</b>\", body_style),\n            Paragraph(\"STOMP over SockJS, WebSockets\", body_style),\n            Paragraph(\"Sub-10ms bi-directional match state sync, countdown ticks, opponent progress, instant verdict alerts\", body_style)\n        ],\n        [\n            Paragraph(\"<b>Backend API</b>\", body_style),\n            Paragraph(\"Java 17, Spring Boot 3.2.5, Spring Security 6\", body_style),\n            Paragraph(\"Stateless JWT authentication, REST endpoints, match state machine, Elo rating recalculations\", body_style)\n        ],\n        [\n            Paragraph(\"<b>Execution Judge</b>\", body_style),\n            Paragraph(\"Custom Java Sandbox (ProcessBuilder, Reflection)\", body_style),\n            Paragraph(\"Isolated process workspaces, memory (256MB) & CPU (2-3s) capping, multi-language execution (Java, C++, Python, JS)\", body_style)\n        ],\n        [\n            Paragraph(\"<b>Persistence & DB</b>\", body_style),\n            Paragraph(\"MySQL 8.0, Spring Data JPA / Hibernate 6, Redis\", body_style),\n            Paragraph(\"ACID relational persistence for 1,000 DSA problems, 5,000 testcases, user stats, Redis fast matchmaking queue\", body_style)\n        ],\n        [\n            Paragraph(\"<b>Automated Tests</b>\", body_style),\n            Paragraph(\"JUnit 5, Mockito, Spring Boot Test\", body_style),\n            Paragraph(\"12/12 automated test suites verifying judge execution, Elo calculations, efficiency engine, and full 1,000-question catalog integrity\", body_style)\n        ]\n    ]\n    stack_table = Table(stack_data, colWidths=[90, 164, 250])\n    stack_table.setStyle(TableStyle([\n        ('BACKGROUND', (0,0), (-1,0), colors.HexColor(\"#f1f5f9\")),\n        ('GRID', (0,0), (-1,-1), 0.5, colors.HexColor(\"#cbd5e1\")),\n        ('TOPPADDING', (0,0), (-1,-1), 5),\n        ('BOTTOMPADDING', (0,0), (-1,-1), 5),\n        ('LEFTPADDING', (0,0), (-1,-1), 6),\n        ('RIGHTPADDING', (0,0), (-1,-1), 6),\n        ('VALIGN', (0,0), (-1,-1), 'TOP'),\n    ]))\n    story.append(stack_table)\n    story.append(Spacer(1, 14))\n    \n    # 3. High-Yield Interview Questions\n    story.append(Paragraph(\"3. High-Yield Technical Interview Questions & Answers\", h1_style))\n    \n    qa_list = [\n        (\n            \"Q1. System Architecture: How does CodeDuel manage real-time 1v1 state synchronization?\",\n            \"<b>Answer</b>: We chose <b>STOMP over WebSockets</b> to achieve full-duplex bi-directional communication with sub-10ms latency. \"\n            \"When two players enter a duel, both subscribe to a private destination <code>/topic/match/{matchId}</code>. \"\n            \"The Spring Boot backend acts as a state machine managing four distinct phases: \"\n            \"<br/>• <b>COUNTDOWN</b>: Broadcasts synchronous 3-2-1 timer ticks before unlocking Monaco Editor. \"\n            \"<br/>• <b>IN_PROGRESS</b>: Relays live typing heartbeats (progress bars) without leaking code content. \"\n            \"<br/>• <b>SUBMISSION_EVALUATION</b>: The judge sandbox runs test cases asynchronously and pushes live PASS/FAIL verdicts. \"\n            \"<br/>• <b>MATCH_COMPLETED</b>: Atomically calculates winner, updates Elo ratings via FIDE formula, and broadcasts match analysis.\"\n        ),\n        (\n            \"Q2. Security & Sandbox: How do you safely execute untrusted user code without crashing the host?\",\n            \"<b>Answer</b>: Arbitrary code execution is isolated using a multi-layer process sandbox in <code>ExecutionSandbox.java</code>: \"\n            \"<br/>1. <b>Directory Isolation</b>: Each submission generates a dedicated UUID directory (<code>./judge-sandbox/exec_{uuid}/</code>). \"\n            \"<br/>2. <b>Process Timeout Enforcing</b>: Processes run via <code>ProcessBuilder</code> with strict timeout bounds (2.0s–3.0s) managed by <code>process.waitFor(timeoutMs, TimeUnit.MILLISECONDS)</code>. Infinite loops trigger <code>process.destroyForcibly()</code>. \"\n            \"<br/>3. <b>Memory Capping</b>: JVM options (<code>-Xmx256m</code>) and OS resource limits prevent memory exhaustion. \"\n            \"<br/>4. <b>Automatic Garbage Cleanup</b>: Temporary binaries and source files are purged in a guaranteed <code>finally</code> block.\"\n        ),\n        (\n            \"Q3. Dynamic Reflection Judge: How does your single judge handle 1,000 questions with varying method signatures?\",\n            \"<b>Answer</b>: Rather than writing separate runner harnesses for each problem, we built dynamic reflection invocation: \"\n            \"<br/>• <b>Java</b>: The wrapper inspects <code>Solution.class.getDeclaredMethods()</code>, dynamically extracts parameter types (<code>int[]</code>, <code>int</code>, <code>String</code>, <code>boolean</code>), parses inputs from <code>Scanner</code> accordingly, invokes <code>solve(...)</code>, and formats the output (e.g. booleans to 'true'/'false', integer arrays to space-separated values). \"\n            \"<br/>• <b>Python</b>: Uses <code>inspect.signature(Solution().solve)</code> to inspect argument count and unpack inputs cleanly.\"\n        ),\n        (\n            \"Q4. Matchmaking Algorithm: How do you pair players fairly and prevent concurrency race conditions?\",\n            \"<b>Answer</b>: Matchmaking uses an <b>expanding Elo-bracket queue</b>. When a player queues: \"\n            \"<br/>1. The system searches for active opponents within ±100 Elo points. \"\n            \"<br/>2. Every 5 seconds without a match, the search window expands to ±250 and ±500 points. \"\n            \"<br/>3. If the queue threshold expires (10s), an automated benchmark opponent of equivalent rating is spawned to guarantee zero dead lobbies. \"\n            \"<br/>4. <b>Thread Safety</b>: Pairing operations use synchronized blocks and atomic locks to guarantee a user is never matched into two concurrent duels simultaneously.\"\n        ),\n        (\n            \"Q5. Elo Rating Math: What formula governs rating updates and rank tiers?\",\n            \"<b>Answer</b>: We implement the standard competitive Elo rating formula: \"\n            \"<br/>• Expected win probability: <code>E_A = 1 / (1 + 10^((R_B - R_A) / 400))</code> \"\n            \"<br/>• New Rating: <code>R'_A = R_A + K * (S_A - E_A)</code> where <code>S_A ∈ {1.0 (win), 0.5 (draw), 0.0 (loss)}</code>. \"\n            \"<br/>• <b>Dynamic K-Factor</b>: New players have K=32 for fast placement; Masters have K=16 for rating stability. \"\n            \"<br/>• Multipliers are awarded for consecutive win-streaks and high Efficiency Engine scores.\"\n        ),\n        (\n            \"Q6. Efficiency Engine: How is the 0–100 code efficiency score computed?\",\n            \"<b>Answer</b>: The efficiency score is a composite weighted metric: \"\n            \"<br/>• <b>Runtime Speed (40%)</b>: Normalized percentile against problem time limit. \"\n            \"<br/>• <b>Memory Consumption (30%)</b>: Evaluated against the 256MB allocation cap. \"\n            \"<br/>• <b>AST / Code Complexity (30%)</b>: Evaluates loop nesting and recursion depth via heuristic analysis to reward optimal O(N) / O(log N) single passes over O(N^2) quadratic nested loops.\"\n        ),\n        (\n            \"Q7. Frontend Performance: How is Monaco Editor integrated with persistent language preferences?\",\n            \"<b>Answer</b>: Monaco Editor (VS Code engine) is integrated via <code>@monaco-editor/react</code>. \"\n            \"<br/>• <b>Language Preference Persistence</b>: When a user selects Java or C++, their preference is saved in <code>localStorage.getItem('codeduel_preferred_language')</code>. Opening any subsequent question, refreshing, or joining a duel immediately loads their chosen language template and method signature. \"\n            \"<br/>• <b>Debounced Draft Autosaving</b>: Code keystrokes are debounced (400ms) and cached locally to prevent accidental progress loss.\"\n        ),\n        (\n            \"Q8. Styled Typography: How did you eliminate raw markdown artifacts in the problem explorer?\",\n            \"<b>Answer</b>: We developed a custom rich-text parser (<code>FormattedContent</code>) in React: \"\n            \"<br/>• <code>**bold**</code> tokens are converted to glowing <b>Amber/Orange badges</b> (<code>text-amber-400 bg-amber-500/10</code>). \"\n            \"<br/>• <code>`code`</code> tokens are converted to <b>Cyan pill